%U A399554 507202816342826871050445640,26923100508889963095874076264544,3096756674868535113859298334327340304,767249895717965576237491529261445041077152
%N A399554 Number of digraphs on n labeled nodes that are reducible for some election of source-SCC headers: some choice of one node per source SCC makes the virtual-rooted flow graph reducible.
%C A399554 An election chooses one node in each source strongly connected component (one receiving no edge from outside). Join a new root to the chosen nodes to obtain a flow graph.
%C A399554 For the election framework see A397965; the choices of distinct source SCCs are independent, so a digraph qualifies iff every non-source SCC has a unique entry and is reducible from it and every source SCC is reducible from at least one node.
%C A399554 All DAGs qualify (any election works on an acyclic digraph).
%C A399554 Each qualifying digraph is counted once, not once for each successful election. All digraphs here have no self-loops.
%C A399554 In the formula, W(m)=A397470(m), V(m)=A401321(m) counts strongly connected digraphs on m labeled nodes reducible from at least one node, and DAG(k) is the set of acyclic digraphs on nodes 1,...,k. src(H) denotes its sources.
%D A399554 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A399554 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A399554 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A399554 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A399554 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A399554/b399554.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..30</a>
%H A399554 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Required Python module (labeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Jul 2026.
%H A399554 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A400123/a400123_1.py.txt">Required Python module (everywhere_reducible.py)</a>, Sep 2026.
%H A399554 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/a401321_1.py.txt">Python program (valid_header_elections.py)</a>, Oct 2026.
%F A399554 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} (1/k!) * Sum_{m_1+...+m_k=n; m_i>=1} multinomial(n;m_1,...,m_k) * Sum_{H in DAG(k)} product_{i in src(H)} V(m_i) * product_{i not in src(H)} m_i*W(m_i) * product_{(i,j) in E(H)} (2^m_i-1).
%o A399554 (Python)
%o A399554 # Save the three linked Python files in one directory using the filenames
%o A399554 # shown in their link captions, then run Python in that directory.
%o A399554 from valid_header_elections import valid_header_sequence
%o A399554 valid_header_sequence("labeled_reducible_digraphs_some", 16)
%Y A399554 Cf. A053763, A003024 (DAGs, all of which qualify), A397965, A397470, A401321.
